\subsection*{3.8.1 Multiplicity Control for Efficacy Analyses}

The trial uses the method of Maurer and Bretz [6] to provide strong multiplicity control for multiple hypotheses as well as interim analyses. Figure 1 shows the initial one-sided \(\alpha\) allocation for each hypothesis in the ellipse representing the hypothesis. The weights for reallocation from each hypothesis to the others are represented in the boxes on the lines connecting hypotheses. This is further explained below.

